","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b210f9596180fe17442eddcdf2c54161d7172f36f1d57f5b1ad576c3ed1cf7c4","event_uuid":"a04c7876-7502-42fd-8bc8-378e62b1412a","position":{"commit_sha":"9ea57e4dfbdaacd152d923124ac2f181d7193b7e","position":"1787115475055079001-a04c7876-7502-42fd-8bc8-378e62b1412a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a2fcbd2e5b342d22b8b79a4a3d38e2415ffc44734680cd95ebd6b98b0ab1161a","event_uuid":"c176a08a-a70d-48b9-8b53-263a0035bc6f","position":{"commit_sha":"394bcfd6b26b7db712af60e23d1543423e985063","position":"1787116265315850001-c176a08a-a70d-48b9-8b53-263a0035bc6f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"13264b7668e4a5922e49c6515955354bcb465ca631c0046c9855379a469eef85","event_uuid":"181388d3-9be7-4d87-9f11-1b93ba32abdc","position":{"commit_sha":"58f589fd2dfebd008843644ce3ba7bb6f6308959","position":"1787116268982250001-181388d3-9be7-4d87-9f11-1b93ba32abdc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787095121445216001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a0b66e1e-c5ea-48d2-b85c-9ef82060be03","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"46e1-2de5-df82-47ea"}],"description":"## Context\nSlice C1 (29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 23 below-seam ambient config reads in the LLM subsystem (`llm/`, `llm/plan_review/`, `llm/workflow/`) as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows, below the composition seam enforced by the in-process AST gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab. Each of the 23, when drained, is STILL FLAGGED (owner=composition in a non-root file); none already owned.\n\nThe 23 reads (relative to `src/rebar/llm/`):\n- `load_config` (12): code_review/workflow_ops.py, completion.py, enrich_drain.py, plan_review/{__init__,det_floor,drift_floor,pin_health,workflow_ops,xcheck}.py, workflow/{completion_banking,gate_dispatch,gate_ops}.py.\n- gate_source.py :: REBAR_GATE_REF, REBAR_GATE_SOURCE, os.environ.get (`_str_pref` feeding `default_ref`/`default_source`).\n- sizing.py :: REBAR_PLAN_REVIEW_BUDGET. usage_log.py :: REBAR_USAGE_LOG. completion_banking.py :: REBAR_ROOT. criterion_preview.py :: REBAR_PREVIEW_TIMEOUT.\n- gate_context.py :: REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED. gate_ops.py :: REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH. executor.py :: os.environ[...]. interpreter.py :: os.environ[...].\n\nAffected SOURCE files: the 21 read-sites plus `config.py`/`_config_sources.py` (owned resolvers) and `config_ownership_exceptions.py` (remove rows). `anthropic_model.py`/`bedrock_model.py` are already roots, untouched.\n\n## Outcome\nEach read gets one treatment and its row is removed. `check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths, no path-glob exception. Behavioral suites stay green; operation-snapshot fingerprints unchanged except recorded deltas.\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (19 reads).** A composed-config read is routed through an OWNED `config.py`/`_config_sources.py` resolver and threaded into the below-seam helper (signature RECEIVES it, or the helper calls the resolver internally where the signature must stay fixed). Timing preserved: a LIVE-per-operation read is cut to a resolver that ALSO re-reads env>file>default each call, so a mid-operation override is never lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via per-line `# read-via:` marker (capped at 4 reads = 4 marked lines).** A read that is NOT composed config (subsystem kill-switch or subprocess/protocol env-control) keeps a marker naming the category. No other listed read may be marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (4 marked lines — the cap)\n1. `gate_context.py` L201 `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED` — audited kill-switch escape hatch for agentic file access outside the snapshot gate. 1 line.\n2. `workflow/gate_ops.py` L196 `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` — kill-switch disabling verify prefetch for the story-a9dd A/B baseline. 1 line.\n3. `workflow/executor.py` L442 `os.environ[...]` — workflow `${VAR}` interpolation named by a spec (protocol env-control), raising if unset. 1 line.\n4. `workflow/interpreter.py` L206 `os.environ[...]` — same `${VAR}` interpolation. 1 line.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add/confirm owned resolvers. REBAR_ROOT in completion_banking is cut to a NEW owned `_config_sources.resolve_run_root(explicit)` for the run-scoped scratch base — precedence explicit>REBAR_ROOT>`Path.cwd()`, with **NO git-toplevel step and NOT realpath-normalized** — mirroring the current `CriterionBank._open`/`for_run` fallback verbatim so the bank dir and repo-leak guard are byte-for-byte unchanged. This is deliberately NOT `repo_root()` (explicit>REBAR_ROOT>git-toplevel>cwd), which would relocate the bank to the git toplevel from a subdir with REBAR_ROOT unset. Add live-per-call `resolve_gate_ref(root)`/`resolve_gate_source(root)` (move `gate_source._str_pref` into the owned seam, env>`[snapshot]`>default), `resolve_plan_review_budget()`, `resolve_usage_log_sink()`, `resolve_preview_timeout()` — each preserving exact precedence/clamping, live per call.\n2. Cut the 19 composed-config reads through those resolvers, threading values into helpers (or calling the resolver internally where a signature must stay fixed). The 12 `load_config` reads use `compose_config(root)` at the gate's per-operation composition point.\n3. Mark the 4 owned-in-place reads; no other markers. Remove the 23 rows. Run the gate + regression set; keep green. Changed call sites are re-derived (Serena `find_referencing_symbols` + a string `grep`) and brought into scope, or the helper reads the resolver internally.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py` (gate scripts imported by BARE name) asserts: (i) `check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding for the 21 listed paths; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries for a listed file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers total exactly 4, confined to gate_context.py/gate_ops.py/executor.py/interpreter.py (1 each). Plus a live-per-call timing regression: a mid-run override of the cut env vars is still observed after the cut (live-per-call, not compose-once). Regression suites kept green: plan_review, workflow, the REBAR_GATE_REF/SOURCE + REBAR_PLAN_REVIEW_BUDGET + REBAR_USAGE_LOG + REBAR_PREVIEW_TIMEOUT + REBAR_ROOT consumer suites, and lifecycle plan-review/gate suites — each injects via the new signature/resolver keeping its assertions.\n\n## Portability & rollback\nThe gate is in-process AST (no CI-provider trigger); resolvers and markers add no CI dependency. No stored format changes. Rollback = revert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No ambient config read remains below the seam in the 21 listed files: 19 cut-to-seam through owned resolvers (live-per-call where the original was live); the 4 enumerated owned-in-place reads carry a per-line `# read-via:` marker (4 lines); no other read marked.\n- [x] The 23 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows removed and `check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception, proven by the held-out `test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py` incl. its marker-total==4 / per-file-placement check.\n- [x] The Testing regression suites pass, including the live-per-call timing regression; operation-snapshot fingerprints unchanged except deltas recorded as a comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerated env-var registry after relocating reads to owned seams."},{"path":"scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py","reason":"Remove the 23 C3d llm LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS rows as reads are cut to seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"Owned live-per-call resolvers for the cut llm reads; re-exported from config."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Owned live-per-call resolvers for the cut llm reads; re-exported from config."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/drift_floor.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pin_health.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/xcheck.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/interpreter.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out seam-clean + live-per-call proof for the llm files."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"],["relates_to","46e1-2de5-df82-47ea"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","parent_status_uuid":"c176a08a-a70d-48b9-8b53-263a0035bc6f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.3.d — llm-workflow cutover: route below-seam config reads through seams","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4f3b65fc-380a-4a88-82fe-f9379c83b926","220ad8e0-0d02-483c-b6c0-3415f4f4c827","03697c74-e567-47cf-a248-fe82b8a59414","e64efa7f-2a39-487c-ba9f-1d4cb80ca413","8f127d7d-a5